Under Clause 5.2 the information security policy must:

- be appropriate to the purpose of the organization;  
- include information‑security objectives (or a framework for setting them);  
- contain a commitment to satisfy applicable information‑security requirements;  
- contain a commitment to continual improvement of the ISMS;  
- be documented;  
- be communicated within the organization;  
- be made available to interested parties as appropriate.

Clause 9.1 requires an organization to determine:

a) what needs to be monitored and measured (including information‑security processes and controls);  
b) the methods for monitoring, measurement, analysis and evaluation to ensure valid results;  
c) when the monitoring and measuring shall be performed;  
d) who shall monitor and measure;  
e) when the results from monitoring and measurement shall be analysed and evaluated;  
f) who shall analyse and evaluate these results.
